submission:
  title: "EnergyOS — Renewable Intelligence Platform"  # REQUIRED — Project display name

  problem_statement: >                 # REQUIRED — 1-3 sentences. What problem? Who has it?
    Renewable energy generation is inherently intermittent — solar output falls
    when clouds pass or after sunset, and wind generation fluctuates with wind
    speed. Grid operators must simultaneously forecast demand spikes, detect
    underperforming assets, diagnose root causes across a mixed renewable fleet
    (wind, solar, hydro, battery), and balance inter-regional power flow — all
    under time pressure using disconnected tools, leading to unnecessary
    curtailment, revenue loss, and avoidable grid instability.

  solution_summary: >                  # REQUIRED — 1-3 sentences. What did you build?
    EnergyOS is an AI-powered single-page web application that unifies five
    intelligent modules — demand spike forecasting, load balancing, anomaly
    detection, root cause analysis, and auto-generated operator briefs — into
    one seamless grid operations platform. It features 36 fully populated
    interactive charts across 6 pages and turns complex energy data into clear,
    actionable decisions that help operators reduce renewable-energy curtailment
    and improve overall grid efficiency.

  key_features:                        # REQUIRED — List 3 to 5 specific features you implemented
    - "AI-powered demand spike forecasting with 12h/24h/7-day windows, confidence intervals, spike event detection, model accuracy tracking (MAPE/RMSE), and forecasted generation-mix charts"
    - "Intelligent load balancing engine with regional load vs capacity analysis, grid health radar, 7-day curtailment history, and prioritised one-click-approve balancing actions"
    - "ML-powered anomaly detection across all renewable assets with severity trend charts, confidence histograms, per-asset time-series drill-down, and deviation-vs-confidence scatter plots"
    - "Automated per-asset root cause analysis with fault trees, cause probability radar, output vs capacity charts, and targeted O&M recommendations"
    - "Auto-generated operator briefs with executive summary, critical anomaly alerts, curtailment minimisation plan, action timeline, and revenue-impact projections"

  tech_stack:
    languages: ["HTML5", "CSS3", "JavaScript (ES6+)"]
    frameworks: ["Vanilla JavaScript (modular IIFE pattern)", "Chart.js 4.4"]
    ibm_technologies: ["IBM Bob (AI pair-programming used throughout development)"]
    databases: ["No database — synthetic data layer (src/assets/js/core/data.js)"]
    other: ["Python http.server (local serving)", "Git", "GitHub", "Chart.js CDN"]

  what_we_are_most_proud_of: >         # Optional but recommended — guides judges to your best work
    EnergyOS unifies five modules — forecasting, anomaly detection, root-cause
    analysis, load balancing, and operator briefs — into one cohesive workflow
    that normally requires five separate enterprise tools. Every single chart
    panel (36 total across 6 pages) is fully populated with contextually
    accurate synthetic data; no panel is left empty. The key achievement is
    turning complex, multi-dimensional energy grid data into clear, ranked,
    actionable operator decisions that can measurably reduce renewable-energy
    curtailment and improve grid efficiency — all in a zero-dependency,
    no-build-step client-side application.

  known_limitations: >                 # Optional but recommended — be honest about gaps
    Operator recommendations are AI-generated decision-support suggestions and
    require human verification before being applied to a real power grid.
    The prototype is not yet connected to SCADA systems, smart meters, IoT
    sensors, or real renewable-energy equipment — all data is synthetically
    simulated in the browser. There is no persistent backend storage; data
    reseeds on every page refresh. The app must be served over HTTP (not
    opened as a file:// URL) due to fetch() usage for page fragment loading.

